  "id": "three-stage-model",
  "term": "three-stage model",
  "definition": "The three-stage model is a dynamic-equilibrium framework used to understand how paradoxical tensions develop and are managed over time. In this source, it is applied to corporate sustainability to organize how tensions arise, how organizations respond, and how equilibrium is understood across stages.",
